>>
Rule 1 (input dtype should be floating-point or complex: 6–10)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (input dtype must be numeric, not string/dtype objects)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 3 (real floating inputs must be within [-1, 1])
{v_1 : tensor} |= if 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 then min(v_1) ≥ -1 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 4 (integer inputs must be within [-1, 1])
{v_1 : tensor} |= if 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 then min(v_1) ≥ -1 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 5 (boolean inputs must be in {0, 1})
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 6 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 7 (1D vector must have positive length)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) > 0
